  "scope": "CPU-derived complete VM topology latency monitor, retaining pinned forced-GC/root/join/shrink correctness checks. Every population has at least 1000 per-VM cycle samples. P55/P99 are descriptive nearest-rank cycle latencies, not package/build startup times, independent samples, confidence intervals or release admission. Failed runs retain flushed raw JSONL and native failure receipts; original 300/120-second caps remain. Same-input qualified resize-grace producer control, to distinguish new successor-only regression from inherited repeated lifecycle failure. No Linux comparison, no timeout widening and no speedup claim. Diagnostic successor enables one sealed Darwin stack sample after twenty seconds if the exact owned executable is still alive. Sampling time is included in the original deadline. This is additional observation of the retained failure, not a runtime fix or a claim that sampler perturbation resolves liveness.",
